{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ec74515d927f6b2b1a404cfb01cce3d7cd39c820bbca9ebae1a0df6e0ebaf4b7","digest":{"component_or_area":"CLI command structure and bridge subsystem","key_entities":["rebar bridge fsck","rebar bridge check-access","rebar bridge setup","bridge-fsck","bridge-probe","jira-onboard","src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py","src/rebar/schemas/bridge_fsck.schema.json","src/rebar/_engine/jira-capability-probe.py","tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py","tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py"],"problem_keywords":["cli verb rename","bridge noun","backward compatibility","command migration","argparse routing"],"propositions":["Three legacy CLI verbs (bridge-fsck, bridge-probe, jira-onboard) must be renamed to nested noun-based spellings (rebar bridge fsck, rebar bridge check-access, rebar bridge setup) as primary commands.","Old verb spellings remain functional as compatibility entrypoints routed through identical implementation paths without behavioral divergence or forking.","The rename is behavior-preserving: bridge check-access executes the same Jira round-trip as legacy bridge-probe; bridge setup runs the same wizard with identical options and env overlay behavior.","Bridge setup calls bridge check-access as final validation, preserving --no-validate escape hatch and skipping validation when JIRA_API_TOKEN is unset or flag is passed.","All enumerated consumers (help text, scripts, tests, docs, workflows) must be migrated to new spellings, with string-named references (monkeypatch targets, literal command assertions) requiring explicit grep-verified migration.","Schema $id and description fields must be updated; compatibility parity tests exercise both old and new spellings for help output, options, exit status, and stdout/stderr."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1786342873156511319,"uuid":"fc50c412-24f9-4b13-96b5-cd1166e4fdbd"}